<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exemplāris</span></b> , e, adj.
		exemplum. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That serves as a pattern</i> or <i>example</i>, <i>exemplary</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtutes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1, 8, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exemplāres</span></b> , ium, m.
			(i. e. libri), <i>copies</i> (for the usual
			exemplaria), <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 4, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Fronto Ep. ad Anton. 2, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
